The <critical micelle concentration> is the approximate total <surfactant> concentration above which additional <surfactant> predominantly enters <micelles>. Below it, most <surfactant> is present as separate <molecules>; above it, the free-monomer concentration changes much more slowly while the <micelle> population increases.

The crossover occurs when aggregation balances the unfavorable exposure of hydrophobic tails to water against head-group repulsion and the loss of molecular translational <entropy>. **It is an aggregation threshold, not the concentration at which every <molecule> becomes micellar.**

